  <!-- EN: Base chance to parry a melee attack. When a parry is performed the equipped weapon or shield will take damage instead of the wielder. If the parrying pawn passes a critical chance check they will automatically riposte their attacker.\nThe final chance depends on the opponent&apos;s parry skill and equal opponents will always have a 20% chance to parry. The internal formula is:\n\nFinalParryChance = ClampBetweenZeroAndOne(0.2 + DefenderParryChance - AttackerParryChance * (1 + AttackerWeaponMeleeCounterParryBonus)*100%\n\nA pawn that is better skilled in parrying takes less damage from parrying while unarmed and is better at reducing damage taken by their weapon on parry. -->
